---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PhotoBand from '../components/PhotoBand.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="EV Trip Reports is a travel agent for EV road trips. Custom plans a human reviews, sourced charging research, and no payment from charging networks.">
  <section class="band band--tight">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1 class="h1">About</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:20px">A travel agent for EV road trips. You tell us where you’re going and what you drive. We plan the charging.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <PhotoBand name="soda-mountains" alt="Interstate 15 and the Soda Mountains at sunset east of Baker, California" caption="I-15 east of Baker, California, 2012." credit="Carol M. Highsmith, Library of Congress" href="https://www.loc.gov/item/2013630775/" />
  <section class="band band--tight">
    <div class="wrap prose">

      <h2>Who’s Behind It</h2>
      <p>I’m Zak Winnick. I work in EV charging infrastructure. Before that I spent 15 years in hospitality, making sure guests didn’t hit surprises. This is the same job for road trips.</p>

      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>No charging network pays us or reviews a plan. If a stop is a site I have a business connection to, the plan says so. If we ever add affiliate links, they’ll be marked, and they won’t pick your charger.</p>

      <h2>How It Gets Done</h2>
      <p>AI tools do much of the research: pulling station data, checking network locators, and collecting driver reports. They follow the rules on <a href="/methodology/">How We Check</a>. A human reviews every plan before it goes out.</p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>Something at a stop doesn’t match? Email <a href="mailto:support@evtripreports.com">support@evtripreports.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
